WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.706
Hi! I like apples. I like pears. We can join them: I like apples and pears. Today we'll learn four joining words.

2
00:00:11.856 --> 00:00:15.162
And adds two things or ideas together.

3
00:00:15.312 --> 00:00:19.554
But joins two different ideas: I am tired but happy.

4
00:00:19.704 --> 00:00:23.442
Because gives the reason: I ate because I was hungry.

5
00:00:23.592 --> 00:00:28.746
So gives the result: I was hungry, so I ate.

6
00:00:28.896 --> 00:00:32.442
Read both parts first and think how they are linked.

7
00:00:32.592 --> 00:00:36.138
If the second part is the reason, use because.

8
00:00:36.288 --> 00:00:39.522
If the second part is the result, use so.

9
00:00:39.672 --> 00:00:45.954
When joining, say repeated words only once: Tom sings and dances.

10
00:00:46.104 --> 00:00:51.330
Watch out! Rain is the reason, not the result, so we can't use so!

11
00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.162
For a reason, use because.

12
00:00:54.312 --> 00:00:58.938
So it's I took an umbrella because it was raining.

13
00:00:59.088 --> 00:01:08.394
Your turn! I have a cat, ___, a dog. Which one? Pause and think.

14
00:01:08.544 --> 00:01:13.578
Adding the two pets: and. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:13.728 --> 00:01:23.298
Another one! The bag is small, ___, heavy. Which one? Pause and think.

16
00:01:23.448 --> 00:01:29.442
Small yet heavy is a contrast: but. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:29.592 --> 00:01:39.402
Here's another! Sam cried, ___, he fell down. Which one? Pause and think.

18
00:01:39.552 --> 00:01:45.402
Falling down is the reason: because. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:45.552 --> 00:01:55.602
Try one more! It was cold, ___, I wore a jacket. Which one? Pause and think.

20
00:01:55.752 --> 00:02:01.722
Wearing a jacket is the result: so. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:01.872 --> 00:02:11.418
Try one more! I wanted to play, ___, it rained. Which one? Pause and think.

22
00:02:11.568 --> 00:02:17.106
Wanting to play but it rained: but. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:17.256 --> 00:02:27.690
Try one more! Mei is hungry, ___, she did not eat lunch. Which one? Pause and think.

24
00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:33.642
Skipping lunch is the reason: because. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:33.792 --> 00:02:44.250
Try one more! Tom sings. Tom dances. Join them with and. Pause and think.

26
00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:50.706
Say Tom once: Tom sings and dances. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:50.856 --> 00:03:01.002
Last one! I like apples, ___, I do not like pears. Which one? Pause and think.

28
00:03:01.152 --> 00:03:06.785
The ideas are opposite, so but. Did you get it right?

29
00:03:06.935 --> 00:03:12.713
Remember: and adds, but contrasts, because gives the reason and so gives the result.

30
00:03:12.863 --> 00:03:17.177
Use because to say why you like something!

